<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">thrall</ansi>

A thrall is a foe that fell in battle and rose again for the Necromancer's
company (see <ansi fg="command">help necromancer</ansi>). Like an Angel or a Demon it lasts one
battle and is never saved (see <ansi fg="command">help summoning</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">What it is</ansi>

  Who      any foe that fell in the battle, except a boss; the Necromancer
           raises the strongest one that fell. Shown as "risen" and its name
  Health   60% of the foe's, or 85% from level 45
  Fights   with the weapon it died holding, at the level it had, as a
           member of the company: it is aimed, struck and can fall
  Never    casts spells, drops loot, wanders or gives experience when it falls

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">How it is raised</ansi>

Once a battle (twice from level 50), when a foe has fallen and the Necromancer
has the mana (a tenth of its maximum), it chants 2 rounds, and a blow can break
the chant (<ansi fg="command">help interrupts</ansi>). A foe's fall is remembered for the rest of
the battle; a fight that is over forgets it.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">How it ends</ansi>

When the battle ends it crumbles. If the Necromancer falls, it crumbles too; at
60 the Lich's Bargain spends it to keep the Necromancer at 1 health.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help necromancer</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help summoning</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>.
